## Authorization and scoping per resource

*Two distinct checks, always both: **authority** (which actions) and **scoping** (which subset of
data). Scoping is applied **in the query**, never as a post-filter.*

| Resource / action | Profile | Authorized? | Scope (scoping) | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| {{resource-and-verb-e.g.-list-orders}} | {{profile}} | {{yes/no}} | {{filter-applied-in-the-query}} | {{eligibility-gate-or-tier-if-applicable}} |

*A resource outside the requester's scope returns **404, not 403** — its existence is not revealed.
A request without a valid profile is **denied** (fail-closed); a default profile is never assumed.*

