## Errors and codes

*Consistency is what lets the client avoid guessing. An out-of-scope situation is always 404.*

| Situation | Code | Body / message | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| No valid profile | {{401-or-equivalent}} | {{generic-message-without-internal-detail}} | fail-closed |
| No authority for the action | {{403}} | {{generic-message}} | resource exists, action refused |
| Resource out of scope (scoping) | {{404}} | {{generic-message}} | never 403 — does not reveal existence |
| {{business-validation-situation}} | {{422-or-equivalent}} | {{message-with-the-violated-invariant}} | links to `BR-nnn` |

## Mandatory tests

*Without these, the contract is not enforced — only described.*

- [ ] Each listed profile sees exactly the expected subset ("sees / does not see" test per profile).
- [ ] Requests without a profile are denied (fail-open impossible — never `profile ?? "admin"`).
- [ ] A resource out of scope returns 404 instead of 403.
- [ ] Sensitive fields are absent from the response for profiles without authority.
- [ ] Guardrail: a test that walks every endpoint and fails if any exposes data without going
      through authorization/scoping.
- [ ] Live proof: two different profiles see different subsets of real data.

